Problem 3: Monolithic Prompt Token Truncation on "Submit"
The Exact Proof in Your Code:
In api/src/services/submissions/execution.service.ts: Lines 124–143 combine all public AND hidden test cases into a single array (allCases), and lines 159–168 pass all of them into a single aiCodeJudgeService.runSamples() call.
In api/src/libs/prompts/ai-code-judge.prompt.ts: Line 17 explicitly says: "- CONCISE THINKING RULE: ... Do not write step-by-step logs for every test case, otherwise you will hit the token limit and get cut off." Whoever wrote this prompt already experienced this exact bug!
The Real-World Bug: When a problem has 15 to 25 hidden test cases, asking an LLM to output verdicts, stdout, stderr, and explanations for all 25 cases causes the output to hit the max_tokens: 5000 ceiling. The response cuts off midway through test case #14, producing incomplete JSON (which is why llm.service.ts had to add the brace repair hack!).
How to Solve It:
"Run" Mode (Samples): Keep it as 1 single fast call (only 2–3 public tests).
"Submit" Mode (All Cases): Chunk the test cases into small batches (e.g. 3–4 tests per batch). Send them in parallel using Promise.all(), then merge the results. No single request ever exceeds the token limit, and execution finishes faster.
